eval returns nothing relevant,\nthe correct behavior is to say so — before spending a model call — and flag the\nanswer for human review. Design the refusal path first; it is the path every other\nsafeguard falls back to.": "Agent Loops describe a process where an agent observes, decides, acts, and observes again, with the loop's reliability determined by its engineering. Each iteration includes perceiving context, deciding actions, acting through tools, and observing results, where the model only influences the decision step. Effective loops should have clear budgets and stopping conditions and should prioritize refusal paths to avoid false completions.",
  "Question: Summarize the document agent-loops.\n\nTool results so far:\nsummarize_document({\"doc_id\": \"agent-loops\"}) returned:\n[agent-loops] Agent Loops describe a process where an agent observes, decides, acts, and observes again, with the loop's reliability determined by its engineering. Each iteration includes perceiving context, deciding actions, acting through tools, and observing results, where the model only influences the decision step. Effective loops should have clear budgets and stopping conditions and should prioritize refusal paths to avoid false completions.": "{\"tool\": \"answer\", \"args\": {\"text\": \"The document 'agent-loops' discusses Agent Loops, a process where an agent observes, decides, acts, and observes again. Each iteration involves perceiving context, deciding actions, acting through tools, and observing results. The model influences only the decision step. Reliable loops require clear budgets and stopping conditions, prioritizing refusal paths to avoid false completions.\"}}",
